# Build-time settings for the extension. Every line is optional: with none of them set, `npm run build`
# makes an extension that talks to a local Membral (`membral local up`, http://localhost:3000) and
# signs in with the API key you paste into the extension's options page.

# Hosted build. Set to 1 to default to https://membral.me and request host access to that origin only.
# Any other value (or unset) defaults to http://localhost:3000 (plus http://127.0.0.1:3000).
# VITE_MEMBRAL_PROD=1

# Override the default target of either build. Its origin becomes the manifest host permission.
# The Cloud URL saved in the options page overrides this at runtime (the browser asks for access).
# VITE_CLOUD_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional email/password sign-in against a Supabase project. When both are unset (the local default),
# the popup hides the password form and points to the options page for the API key instead.
# For local development, use the URL printed by `npx supabase start`.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
